==============================================================================
agentYY ROUTE 2 — relative/generalized entropy S(a) in the type II_1 algebra
==============================================================================

--- PART A: re-verify the banked modular-temperature identities ---
[A1] Tolman  sqrt(a^2+H^2)*cos u - H = H*(cos(u)/Abs(cos(u)) - 1)  (expect 0)
[A2] T_mod - T_DL = H*(-1/Abs(cos(u)) + 1/cos(u))/(2*pi)  (expect 0)
[A3] T_DL(a) = sqrt(a^2+H^2)/(2 pi) -- the boost-KMS modular temperature.
     dT_DL/da = a/(2*pi*sqrt(H**2 + a**2))  (= a/(2pi sqrt(a^2+H^2)); the F4 susceptibility agentQ flagged)

--- PART B: Araki relative entropy of two KMS states of the boost ---
beta(a) = 2 pi / sqrt(a^2 + H^2);  beta_GH = beta(0) = 2 pi / H
d beta/d a = -2*pi*a/(H**2 + a**2)**(3/2)  (<0: beta DECREASES monotonically in a)
  -> as a grows the local KMS state gets HOTTER; beta runs monotonically a:0->oo, beta:2pi/H->0

--- PART C: model M1 (single boost-mode oscillator) S_rel(a) ---
S_rel(b||bG) = -(Omega*(b - bG) - (exp(Omega*b) - 1)*(Omega*b - Omega*bG - log(exp(Omega*b) - 1) + log(exp(Omega*bG) - 1)))/(exp(Omega*b) - 1)
  check S_rel(bG||bG) = 0  (expect 0)
  dS_rel/db = Omega*(Omega*b*exp(Omega*b) - Omega*bG*exp(Omega*b) - 2*exp(Omega*b) + 2)/(exp(2*Omega*b) - 2*exp(Omega*b) + 1)
  -> = (b-bG)*dU/db ; sign(dS_rel/db)=sign(b-bG) since dU/db<0:
     dU/db = -Omega**2/(4*sinh(Omega*b/2)**2)  (negative for all b,Omega>0)

