--- PART G: is a*/H=1/sqrt(2) thermodynamic or just the kinematic map? ---
  beta(a/H) = 2pi/sqrt((a/H)^2+1)
  d2 beta/d(a/H)^2 = 2*pi*(2*a_H**2 - 1)/(a_H**2 + 1)**(5/2)
  inflection of beta(a/H): a/H = [sqrt(2)/2]
  d2 T_DL/d(a/H)^2 = 1/(2*pi*(a_H**2 + 1)**(3/2))  -> T_DL is CONVEX everywhere, NO inflection (no feature)
  dT_DL/d(a/H) = a_H/(2*pi*sqrt(a_H**2 + 1))  -> monotone increasing, saturates to 1/2pi; no peak

  Compare: beta(a) inflection at a/H = 1/sqrt(2) = 0.7071067811865476
  == the M2 cold-limit a*/H = 0.7071. CONFIRMED: the frozen feature is the
  inflection of the algebraic blueshift map beta=2pi/sqrt(a^2+H^2), i.e. the
  geometric crossover of sqrt(a^2+H^2) -- DESCRIPTIVE, not a derived extremum.

--- PART H: algebra-level Jacobson dQ=T dS_gen -- evade or inherit Q? ---
  T_mod * beta_GH = sqrt(a^2+H^2)/H = sqrt(a_H**2 + 1)  (= 1/|xi|, the pure blueshift)
  => Clausius factor (1 - T_mod beta_GH) = 1 - sqrt(a^2+H^2)/H
     = 1 - 1/|xi|  -- a PURE Tolman blueshift factor, fixed by geometry.
  This is the SAME object agentQ found: the a-dependence is the Tolman factor
  sqrt(a^2+H^2), entering through T_mod, NOT an independent dT/da channel.
  CONCLUSION: the type II_1 ALGEBRA-level Clausius INHERITS agentQ's no-go.
  The modular heat consumes <H_mod>; the only a-dependence is the geometric
  blueshift sqrt(a^2+H^2)=1/|xi| -- exactly the Tolman-trivial factor that
  cancels (R1) or lands anti-MOND (R2). No dT_DL/da inertia-side channel appears.

--- PART I: strict monotonicity of S_rel(a); nothing at a~cH ---
  chain rule: dS_rel/da = (dS_rel/db) * (db/da)
    Correct dS_rel/db = Omega(Omega(b-bG)e^{Omega b} - 2e^{Omega b} + 2)/(1-e^{Omega b})^2
    (verified < 0 for all b<bG; the naive (b-bG)dU/db factorization is INCOMPLETE)
    a>0 => b=beta(a) < bG => dS_rel/db < 0 ;  db/da < 0
    => dS_rel/da = (neg)(neg) = POSITIVE  -- matches the machine scan below.
  dS_rel/da > 0 at every scanned a in [1e-4, 5000]: True (STRICTLY monotone increasing)
  => S_rel(a) has NO extremum. Minimum is at a=0 (the GH state itself, S_rel=0).
  Z=5.789 (a=cH): S_rel and all derivatives are smooth & featureless there
  (d2S changes sign near a*/H~O(1)-O(200) depending on probe; NEVER pinned to Z).

DONE.
